:13679655,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEzNjc5NjU1","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/13679655?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/BManx2000","html_url":"https://github.com/BManx2000","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BManx2000/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BManx2000/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BManx2000/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BManx2000/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BManx2000/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BManx2000/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BManx2000/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BManx2000/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BManx2000/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-03-06T21:38:42Z","updated_at":"2026-03-06T21:38:42Z","body":"I had a look through the code and I believe I've found the problem in this function:\nhttps://github.com/godotengine/godot/blob/220b0b2f74d8e089481b140c42a42992a76dd6fc/modules/navigation_3d/3d/nav_map_builder_3d.cpp#L273\n\n1. It loops through all regions without regard for navigation layers. If multiple regions have a polygon with the same closest distance, it defaults to the first region it found. Adding a check for compatible navigation layers should fix the case in my MRP. But there is another issue:\n2. It will only ever build one connection per link, even if the link would be valid for multiple pairs of regions. This looks like it would be a more involved fix, it would have to make a connection between every valid pair of regions.","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4014293745/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_