ml_url":"https://github.com/BManx2000","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BManx2000/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BManx2000/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BManx2000/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BManx2000/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BManx2000/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BManx2000/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BManx2000/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BManx2000/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BManx2000/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-03-18T18:54:11Z","updated_at":"2026-03-18T18:54:11Z","body":"New MRP I'm testing with. In this version there are 2 agents on different layers which should move in lockstep with each other, but the bug causes one of them to not traverse the links. There is also a 2D scene, as the 2D navigation link code is identical and suffers from the same bug. I will add test cases like this to the unit test suites.\n\n[navigation-link-test2.zip](https://github.com/user-attachments/files/26095992/navigation-link-test2.zip)","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4084904356/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4195226145","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/117138#issuecomment-4195226145","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/117138","id":4195226145,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc76DhIh","user":{"login":"BManx2000","id":13679655,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEzNjc5NjU1","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/13679655?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/BManx2000","html_url":"https://github.com/BManx2000","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BManx2000/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BManx2000/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BManx2000/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BManx2000/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BManx2000/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BManx2000/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BManx2000/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BManx2000/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BManx2000/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-04-06T21:55:06Z","updated_at":"2026-04-06T21:55:06Z","body":"Another MRP for the simplified PR where I only have the navigation layer check and left out the multi-region connection support. In this one the red and green agents should both be able to pathfind to all positions, but by different links.\n\n[navigation-link-test3.zip](https://github.com/user-attachments/files/26521319/navigation-link-test3.zip)","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4195226145/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4259112059","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/117138#issuecomment-4259112059","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/117138","id":4259112059,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc793OR7","user":{"login":"MJacred","id":6639237,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY2MzkyMzc=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/6639237?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/MJacred","html_url":"https://github.com/MJacred","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MJacred/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MJacred/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MJacred/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MJacred/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MJacred/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MJacred/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MJacred/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MJacred/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MJacred/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-04-16T09:57:14Z","updated_at":"2026-04-16T10:01:35Z","body":"After having read most of the navigation code in the engine over the last 2-3 weeks, I can say that **the code works as intended and should not be changed**.\n\nThe fix for your MRP would be: _remove the region with navigation layer 1 toggled_. It's not needed.  \nIf you need agents of different sizes to navigate the same space, you need a different navigation map with the same/similar setup (see [tutorial](https://docs.godotengine.org/en/stable/tutorials/navigation/navigation_different_actor_types.html)).  \nDifferent agent sizes (radius and height) have different needs for their baked navigation mesh.\n\nIn your example, you have **2 regions _of the same map_ that share basically the same navigation mesh** (position- and bounds-wise). They differ in navigation layers, but that is only to be used for querying/finding paths for agents.\n\nWhen a link tries to find points (across all regions of the same map) to connect to, it is interested in the region's position and bounds (and its bounds-check is extended by `link_connection_radius` set in the project settings / in the map: the default is `1.0`). And it should not do any more than that.\n\nAt the top of my hat I can think of 2 reasons why filtering by the link's navigation layers, as you suggested, would cause issues:\n1. changing a link's navigation layers at runtime would cause a resync of the map, _and_ affect all other agents' queries\n2. break the example setup below\n\nusing your MRP as a basis:\n* use just the lower box mesh as `terrain` (1st region) with just navigation layers `1` toggled\n* use the upper box mesh as `platform` (2nd region) with just navigation layers `2` toggled\n* the navigation link has just navigation layers `3` toggled\n\nAny agent with the layers 1, 2, and 3 can move freely from terrain to platform and back.  \nAny agent missing layer 3 would never get up there.\n\nChanging the navigation layers on the agent side is way less impactful\n\n**EDIT**: Extending the class docs is a good idea though.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4259112059/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4263339493","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/117138#issuecomment-4263339493","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/117138","id":4263339493,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7-HWXl","user":{"login":"BManx2000","id":13679655,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEzNjc5NjU1","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/13679655?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/BManx2000","html_url":"https://github.com/BManx2000","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BManx2000/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BManx2000/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BManx2000/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BManx2000/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BManx2000/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BManx2000/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BManx2000/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BManx2000/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BManx2000/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-04-16T20:52:52Z","updated_at":"2026-04-16T20:52:52Z","body":"OK, so I was just doing agent types wrong this whole time, sorry for wasting your time. This method where you have to use the server directly and manually assign everything to maps is really terrible though, I'm probably just going to keep using my custom build and shove everything into the default map to be honest.","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4263339493/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4263416756","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/117138#issuecomment-4263416756","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/117138","id":4263416756,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7-HpO0","user":{"login":"MJacred","id":6639237,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY2MzkyMzc=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/6639237?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/MJacred","html_url":"https://github.com/MJacred","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MJacred/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MJacred/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MJacred/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MJacred/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MJacred/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MJacred/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MJacred/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MJacred/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MJacred/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-04-16T21:06:25Z","updated_at":"2026-04-16T21:06:25Z","body":"You have done nothing wrong, so there's nothing to be sorry about","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4263416756/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null}]